Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:28:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Let the textual-body client stub answer the alias
 lookup

Rendering a room-alias pill resolves the target through findRoomByAlias,
which asks the client for its visible rooms rather than all of them. This
stub is an explicit method list rather than a full fake, so it only
answered the older call and the pill threw mid-render. Pointing both at
the same pair of rooms keeps the two answers consistent, which is what the
shared client fixtures already do.
---
 .../src/components/views/messages/TextualBodyFactory.test.tsx    | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/apps/web/src/components/views/messages/TextualBodyFactory.test.tsx b/apps/web/src/components/views/messages/TextualBodyFactory.test.tsx
index bf3ac2d824..1c97b6f6d4 100644
--- a/apps/web/src/components/views/messages/TextualBodyFactory.test.tsx
+++ b/apps/web/src/components/views/messages/TextualBodyFactory.test.tsx
@@ -93,6 +93,7 @@ describe("<TextualBody />", () => {
                 return null;
             },
             getRooms: () => [defaultRoom, otherRoom],
+            getVisibleRooms: () => [defaultRoom, otherRoom],
             getAccountData: (): MatrixEvent | undefined => undefined,
             isGuest: () => false,
             mxcUrlToHttp: (s: string) => s,
